{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>He sent</b> — Perhaps the questioner will ask: if darkness is an event, how can it be a messenger? Perhaps this questioner will wake from his sleep and see: so will be my word that goes out from my mouth — the one I sent." "<b>And they darkened</b> — Scripture mentions above the land of Ham." "<b>And they did not rebel</b> — They did not rebel against Moses and Aaron, or against His signs. And He mentioned the plague of darkness, because on its account Pharaoh gave permission to go to serve HaShem, and afterward He returned to mention the plagues and began from the first."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {0 "The phrase כן יהיה דברי אשר יצא מפי appears to quote Isaiah 55:11; אשר שלחתיו at the end is textually awkward — translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:32.041906372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}